From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ciscobugger <xizko55@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] mm/page_alloc: never count more free CMA than the zone
 holds

Workaround for a counter drift seen on this machine, not a root-cause fix.

During uptime NR_FREE_CMA_PAGES grows far past the only CMA pool (the
device tree's 128 MB linux,cma, 32768 pages): 34013 against 11642 pages
really free on the CMA free lists, and 111 in the DMA zone, which holds no
CMA pageblocks at all. The pool itself is fine; only the counter drifts.

__zone_watermark_unusable_free() adds NR_FREE_CMA_PAGES to the unusable
free memory of every allocation that cannot use CMA. With the drifted
counter usable free memory goes negative: kswapd and GFP_ATOMIC
allocations fail ("page allocation failure", ath12k rx buffers -12) and
the desktop freezes with gigabytes available and zram unused.

Cap the value at zone_cma_pages() in the watermark check and in the
__rmqueue CMA balance. With a correct counter the result is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: ciscobugger <xizko55@gmail.com>
---
 mm/page_alloc.c | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mm/page_alloc.c b/mm/page_alloc.c
index ee902a468..eac894fdf 100644
--- a/mm/page_alloc.c
+++ b/mm/page_alloc.c
@@ -2463,7 +2463,7 @@ __rmqueue(struct zone *zone, unsigned int order, int migratetype,
 		 * is in the CMA area.
 		 */
 		if (alloc_flags & ALLOC_CMA &&
-		    zone_page_state(zone, NR_FREE_CMA_PAGES) >
+		    min(zone_page_state(zone, NR_FREE_CMA_PAGES), zone_cma_pages(zone)) >
 		    zone_page_state(zone, NR_FREE_PAGES) / 2) {
 			page = __rmqueue_cma_fallback(zone, order);
 			if (page)
@@ -3569,9 +3569,15 @@ static inline long __zone_watermark_unusable_free(struct zone *z,
 		unusable_free += READ_ONCE(z->nr_free_highatomic);
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_CMA
-	/* If allocation can't use CMA areas don't use free CMA pages */
+	/*
+	 * If allocation can't use CMA areas don't use free CMA pages. Never count
+	 * more than the zone's CMA pages: on the Book4 Edge (X1P42100) the
+	 * NR_FREE_CMA_PAGES counter drifts far past the 128 MB pool during uptime,
+	 * which made usable free negative and starved kswapd and atomic allocations.
+	 */
 	if (!(alloc_flags & ALLOC_CMA))
-		unusable_free += zone_page_state(z, NR_FREE_CMA_PAGES);
+		unusable_free += min(zone_page_state(z, NR_FREE_CMA_PAGES),
+				     zone_cma_pages(z));
 #endif
 
 	return unusable_free;
